# Backend

All server code is Go under `backend/`. Layout: `docs/architecture/directory-structure.md`.

- Handlers are the HTTP adapter. They bind DTOs, call an `internal/services` interface, and return `dto.Success` or `mapError`. They do not import logic or repositories.
- `internal/services` declares those interfaces and does not implement them. Events and third-party adapters call the same interfaces.
- Feature logic lives in `internal/logic/**` and implements the service interfaces, including one derivation of inventory age and stock state.
- Repositories own queries and commands. Use `ErrValidation`, `ErrNotFound`, and `ErrConflict`.
- Register routes only in `internal/app/routes/v1/routes.go`.
- Calendar dates are `DATE` / `YYYY-MM-DD`. JSON tags are snake_case.

In stock means `stockedOutOn == nil`. Keep domain logic out of `main.go`, middleware, and DTOs.

Logging uses zap (`pkg/logger`). Middleware sets `trace_id` on the request context (`X-Trace-ID`); handlers, logic, and repositories log via `logger.FromContext(ctx)`.
